    "explanation": "<p class=\"text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground\">Simplifying surds involves rewriting a square root in its simplest form by identifying perfect square factors inside the root and taking them out. For example, √12 can be rewritten by splitting into √(4 × 3) = √4 × √3 = 2√3.</p>",
